## provision.verify · cli absent · plugin present
   ✋ ConstraintError: the aws cli is absent from PATH
      ⇒ no aws identity can answer on this box, and from a laptop no ec2
        grove can be woken — git.grove.wake opens its tunnel through
        'aws ssm start-session' (a tailnet grove's wake needs no aws)
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply
   • the ssm session-manager plugin is present ✔
rc=1

## provision.verify · cli adrift · plugin present
   ✋ ConstraintError: aws is v2, and NOT at the version this repo declares
      ⇒ two boxes then run different cli code from one unchanged
        line — the deterministic clause of one-command provision
      ⇒ a command -v guard cannot see a version at all, so a
        presence check reports this state nowhere
      read why: aws --version
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply
           its upsert re-runs the installer with --update
   • the ssm session-manager plugin is present ✔
rc=1

## provision.verify · cli v1 · plugin present
   ✋ ConstraintError: the aws on PATH is NOT v2
      ⇒ debian's awscli package is v1, which answers command -v
        and then fails every v2-only call with an opaque arg error
      ⇒ a presence-check guard counts it done and skips, so this
        line would name a re-apply that could never clear it
      read why: aws --version ; type -a aws
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply
           its upsert installs v2 over it, and says so when a v1
           earlier on PATH still shadows the result
   • the ssm session-manager plugin is present ✔
rc=1

## provision.verify · cli whole · plugin absent
   • aws cli is v2 at the declared version ✔
   ✋ ConstraintError: the ssm session-manager plugin is absent
      ⇒ 'aws ssm start-session' fails with 'SessionManagerPlugin is
        not found' — the cli alone cannot open a session
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply
rc=1

## provision.verify · cli whole · plugin present
