## provision.upsert · the fetch of *.zip fails
   💥 MalfunctionError: could not fetch the aws cli installer
      ⇒ with no aws cli, no ec2 grove can be woken — git.grove.wake
        opens its tunnel through 'aws ssm start-session' (a tailnet grove's needs no aws)
rc=1

## provision.upsert · the fetch of *.zip.sig fails
   💥 MalfunctionError: could not fetch the aws cli installer's signature
      ⇒ the zip is discarded UNOPENED. an unverifiable installer
        would run as root, having proven not one fact about its bytes
rc=1

## provision.upsert · the fetch of *session-manager-plugin.deb fails
   • aws cli already at the declared version; skipped (whole)
   💥 MalfunctionError: could not install the ssm plugin from https://s3.amazonaws.com/session-manager-downloads/plugin/1.2.835.0/ubuntu_64bit/session-manager-plugin.deb
      ⇒ 'aws ssm start-session' then fails with 'SessionManagerPlugin
        is not found', so no grove tunnel can open
rc=1

## provision.upsert · the fetch of *session-manager-plugin.deb.sig fails
   • aws cli already at the declared version; skipped (whole)
   💥 MalfunctionError: could not fetch the ssm plugin's signature
      ⇒ the .deb is discarded UNINSTALLED. a .deb's maintainer
        procedures run as ROOT, so an unverified package is not a
        lesser install — it is arbitrary root code
rc=1

## provision.upsert · the extract fails
   • aws cli 2.36.23 verified against aws's signer key ✔
   💥 MalfunctionError: could not extract the aws cli installer
      ⇒ it said: unzip: cannot find or open the zip
      ⇒ unzip may be absent; a fresh ubuntu image ships none
      fix: sudo apt install unzip, then re-apply — rhx grove.provision --what 5.6.aws --mode apply
rc=1

## provision.upsert · the installer fails
   • aws cli 2.36.23 verified against aws's signer key ✔
   💥 MalfunctionError: the aws cli installer failed, so no aws cli landed
      ⇒ it said: install: permission denied
      read why: ls -ld /usr/local/aws-cli /usr/local/bin ; df -h /usr/local
rc=1

## provision.upsert · the install lands, a v1 shadows it
   • aws cli 2.36.23 verified against aws's signer key ✔
   💥 MalfunctionError: the installer ran, and the aws on PATH is still 'v1'
      ⇒ v2 landed at /usr/local/bin/aws. another aws earlier on PATH
        shadows it — debian's 'awscli' package (v1) is the usual one
      read why: type -a aws ; echo "$PATH"
rc=1

## provision.upsert · apt refuses the plugin package
   • aws cli already at the declared version; skipped (whole)
